a bitter gravecap fungus~
A pale bitter gravecap fungus grows from the damp mortar.~
The pallid fungus thrives where mineral water seeps through old burial
stone. Its flesh smells sharply medicinal and leaves a numbing residue
on the fingers. Sewer scavengers know better than to eat it without
preparation.
~
